238
00:09:59,098 --> 00:10:00,600
[Maya] See, he's smiling to you.

239
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:03,102
-You like the blonde girl?
-[Aiden giggles]

240
00:10:03,185 --> 00:10:06,439
-See? He's relaxed with you, I mean...
-Who's a baby?

241
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:07,815
You're good, girl. You're ready.

242
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:11,027
-[Heather] Oh! Spit up.
-[Maya] Oh, shit.

243
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:12,820
-Holy moly.
-I know.

244
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:15,156
I'm so excited to see Maya as a mom.

245
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:16,824
I'm just so proud of her

246
00:10:16,907 --> 00:10:20,536
and her struggles with getting pregnant
and the miscarriages.

247
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:25,124
So to see her as a mom and she finally got
everything that she's been hoping for,

248
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:27,209
I'm so happy for her.

249
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:29,045
And Aiden is so cute.

250
00:10:29,128 --> 00:10:31,547
I tried to look on Instagram to see 
what's going on in your life

251
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,424
and text you guys, but it's hard.

252
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,468
I was in a weird zone, too
because it was like,

253
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:38,012
going through a breakup and then dating,

254
00:10:38,095 --> 00:10:40,473
I've been in this, like, bubble of love.

255
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:43,017
You didn't tell me, girl, and then
I see you on TMZ, I'm like...

256
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,936
[Heather] It happened really fast with us,
and we just, like--

257
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:47,229
He's literally my best friend.

258
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:49,231
So how did you guys meet?

259
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:50,316
Fourth of July.

260
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:55,112
His boat was parked next
to the boat I was on down in Newport.

261
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:56,197
-Really?
-And my girlfriend

262
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:57,573
just happened to be on his boat.

263
00:10:57,656 --> 00:11:00,660
I jumped on his boat and he turned around

264
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:02,828
and he was like, "Hi, I'm Tarek."

265
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:05,456
Then we were just texting 
and kept in touch.

266
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,666
On our first date, it was just like...

267
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:09,960
-[Maya] Magic?
-It was like...

268
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:13,172
I found him very endearing 
and very, like, kind and real.

269
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:15,007
I feel, like, really good.

270
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:17,218
We've been dating for about a month.

271
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:19,387
So it definitely moved very quick.

272
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:22,890
But we both said that when we're together
the world stops.

273
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:25,935
I feel like I've known him for years.

274
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:27,603
Doesn't feel like it's only been a month.

275
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:29,397
Bu when you know, you know, right?

276
00:11:30,272 --> 00:11:31,607
And how are things at the office?

277
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:33,317
Christine's situation was--

278
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:37,405
So, wait. I missed everything.
Like, I'm in Miami, right?

279
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,448
I was in Sweden. [laughing]

280
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:41,534
So, I get a call from Davina,

281
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:43,953
saying, "You heard
that Christine is engaged?"

282
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:45,413
I'm like, "What? Engaged?"

283
00:11:45,496 --> 00:11:48,207
I'm like, "Wait a minute.
I saw Christine in December.

284
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:51,585
-And she said she's dating this guy..."
-The younger guy.

285
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,713
Yeah! But then, I guess she met Christian,

286
00:11:53,796 --> 00:11:56,465
and two months later in February, I get...

287
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:57,508
-Engaged.
-Yeah.

288
00:11:57,591 --> 00:12:01,262
It's funny, she judged Mary 
for rushing with Romain.

289
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:05,891
I'm shocked, but I'm so happy for her
and her ring is freaking stunning.

290
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:07,852
What's going on with 
Christine and Chrishell?

291
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:10,104
Are they still kind of like, not talking?

292
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:11,021
Well...

293
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,066
It makes me so uncomfortable

294
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:17,236
because I just feel the tension. 
I don't know how to...

295
00:12:17,319 --> 00:12:19,530
-...deal with it. Yeah.
-Between the two?

296
00:12:19,613 --> 00:12:22,283
I feel like it's just time to--
It's been so long now.

297
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:25,119
I don't even think at this point
they know what they're fighting about.

298
00:12:25,202 --> 00:12:26,078
Like, it's done, it's over.

299
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:28,539
Mary's not even mad about anything,
and it was about Mary.

300
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:30,750
-That's the funny thing.
-Shouldn't Mary be the one upset?

301
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:32,793
I know, that's the whole thing.

302
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:35,379
Christine was fighting about Mary,
Mary doesn't even care.

303
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:39,258
And it's been a couple of months,
and I mean, we all have the same goals.

304
00:12:39,341 --> 00:12:41,552
To sell houses and 
actually do real estate.

305
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:42,553
-You know?
-Yeah.

306
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:44,263
-[baby groaning]
-He's getting fussy, girl.

307
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:45,347
-Is he? Okay.
-Yeah.

308
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,640
-Ready to bounce?
-Yeah.

309
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:49,769
-I want him, he's so cute, Maya.
-He's a good baby.

310
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:52,855
But honestly, I'm excited to come to 
the office and dress up,

311
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:55,065
and not have clothes
with my baby spit on it.

312
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:57,693
-[Heather gasps]
-Yeah, sorry about that girl.

313
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:59,528
Send me the bill for the dry clean.

314
00:12:59,612 --> 00:13:00,821
[both laughing]

315
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:07,495
♪ Oh, oh
See the future with my head up high ♪

316
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:09,705
♪ Like a flame on my mind, I multiply ♪

317
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:11,415
[engine roaring]

318
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:16,712
Do you guys always get kicked off 
the Wi-Fi? It's really frustrating.

319
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:19,340
Ooh! Oh, my goodness, I just...

320
00:13:19,423 --> 00:13:20,382
slid into my desk.

321
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:22,343
[Brett] Chrishell, I've got your husband
on my desk.

322
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:24,220
Okay, not this one right?

323
00:13:24,303 --> 00:13:25,846
[Brett laughing] Nice plug.

324
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,807
[Chrishell] I got my reading materials.

325
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:30,017
We should put pictures
of our men on our desks.

326
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,602
Thank God I'm married to him,

327
00:13:31,685 --> 00:13:34,772
because I would be like, "Oh, my God."

328
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:36,732
[Mary] Is that weird to think that

329
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:41,153
there are some teenage girls that actually
have his picture up on their wall?

330
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,906
-No, I think it's, like, a compliment.
-[Mary] Yeah.

331
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:44,824
[Mary] It's cute.

332
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:47,952
Yeah. Because it's like, 
"I know where he sleeps." [chuckles]

333
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:48,911
Most nights.

334
00:13:49,703 --> 00:13:54,124
Oh, Brett, you're just jealous because
you've got the rotating door going on.

335
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:55,292
Not anymore.

336
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:57,461
I'm a one-woman man for the last 48 hours.

337
00:13:58,212 --> 00:13:59,421
A one-woman man?

338
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:00,714
Forty-eight hours.

339
00:14:01,131 --> 00:14:01,966
Who's the girl?

340
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:04,385
[Brett] This girl from the party
hasn't left yet.

341
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:06,595
You've allowed her to stay for this long?

342
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,513
[Brett] Yeah.

343
00:14:09,014 --> 00:14:11,016
I mean, she'll be gone tomorrow, forever.
[laughing]

344
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:13,602
I mean,
this is your longest relationship ever.

345
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:16,605
No, Ernestine, my housekeeper. 
Four years, three years.

346
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:17,690
Oh, my gosh.

347
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:20,693
-[Chrishell] Do you have a second?
-Yeah, sure.

348
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:22,945
I wanna talk to you about
something real quick.

349
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,488
[Chrishell] I'm excited to tell you.

350
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,992
Um, I know you always joke

351
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:30,786
about needing to have a passport
to go to the Valley,

352
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:34,039
but I feel like it's constant construction

353
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,041
and there's a lot of new builds.
I feel like,

354
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:38,836
why don't I focus a little more over there

355
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:40,754
'cause I already know the area,
I live there.

356
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:41,881
I know the school system.

357
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:45,467
My husband Justin and I just bought 
our dream home in the Valley

358
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:46,635
and we love it so much.

359
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,554
It's like this modern farmhouse 

360
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:52,391
that really feels like 
an oasis outside of the city

361
00:14:52,474 --> 00:14:55,686
and it's something that I never
really even dreamed of.

362
00:14:55,769 --> 00:14:57,771
We realized, this is where it's at.

363
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:59,106
I'm big on the Valley.

364
00:14:59,189 --> 00:15:01,650
I've been hearing about it,
but the price points are going up.

365
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:04,194
It used to be one, two-million dollar
sales and now I'm seeing

366
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:06,989
three, four, five, six, seven, 
ten-million dollar sales out there.

367
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:09,909
-Right.
-You've been looking at developments?

368
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:11,911
-Yeah, I've actually been--
-You have a positive take?

369
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:14,204
Not knocking, because some of them
don't have doors,

370
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:18,876
but I'll see a construction site and I'll
go up and drop off some material.

371
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:21,712
I've yet to get a listing, but I wanna get
one of these new builds.

372
00:15:21,795 --> 00:15:24,381
One builder is doing like
seven things normally,

373
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,508
so I'm trying to get my foot in the door.

374
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:30,304
There's really no brokerage controlling
a lot of the business out there.

375
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:32,973
So I think we can go out there,
do what we do over here,

376
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:34,975
and I think everyone 
will love us out there.

377
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:36,769
We need you to be 
the front person for this.

378
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:38,687
That'd be great. I would really love that.

379
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:41,982
Okay, so the Valley might not be 
as cool to Jason and Brett

380
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:45,819
as the sexy Hollywood Hills,
but there are a lot of commissions.

381
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:47,488
Really good commissions
that you can make

382
00:15:47,571 --> 00:15:49,031
on the other side of the hill.

383
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:52,493
I'm going to keep driving around
and trying to get listing appointments

384
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:53,827
with the different developers.

385
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:56,246
Listen, if you can get
one foot in the door,

386
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:58,165
then I'll drive over there 
and we'll close it.

387
00:15:58,248 --> 00:16:00,709
Did you think you'd ever say that?
You used to make fun of me 

388
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:03,170
-for thinking the Valley was cool.
-That's why you're here.

389
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:06,590
I'm seriously withholding a lot of jokes
about the Valley now because I'm--

390
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,092
-See?
-I'm far more about it.

391
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:10,177
Wait, so hold on a second, 
are you saying...

392
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:11,553
Was I right?

393
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:14,056
-I will--
-[Brett] We don't need to go that far.

394
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:16,308
I'm really glad you talked about this,

395
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:18,185
because this is more exciting for me
than for you.

396
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:19,436
I'm up for the challenge.

397
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,647
-Yeah, thank you. We're on the same page.
-I love it.

398
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:23,232
♪ You better get ready
Because I'm breaking out? ♪

399
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:25,526
♪ You better get ready for what I got ♪

400
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:28,404
♪ If you ain't ready
You ain't keeping up ♪

401
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:29,321
[Amanza] Ooh!

402
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:30,572
Honey, I'm home.

403
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,992
-Wow! [chuckles]
-[Mary] Right?

404
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,035
[Amanza] Mary,
I'm glad you have to hop out.

405
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:36,662
[Mary] Yeah, Jason...

406
00:16:36,745 --> 00:16:39,081
Why did we not bring the Rolls?

407
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:41,250
[Jason] This is the Rolls Royce
of Broncos.

408
00:16:41,333 --> 00:16:45,212
[Mary] You're going to have to wear heels
one day so you have to actually do this.

409
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:49,967
[Mary] Jason has wanted this Bronco 
for his whole life basically 

410
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:52,761
and he spent like $200,000

411
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:55,014
restoring it and getting it built

412
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:57,683
custom to exactly his taste.

413
00:16:57,766 --> 00:16:58,976
[Amanza] I'm already sweating.

414
00:16:59,059 --> 00:17:02,563
If I had $200,000
to just throw at something 

415
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:05,399
then it would most definitely be a house.

416
00:17:05,482 --> 00:17:08,110
But you know how boys are,
 they love their toys.

417
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:11,780
[Jason] So Amanza, sometimes you have
to preview a property for your client.

418
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:14,324
So that's what Mary and I are doing here.

419
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:18,078
Make sure the floor plan is good,

420
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:20,664
make sure the views are good, 
it's private, things like that,

421
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:22,124
before our client wastes his time.

422
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:25,586
I met Mary and Jason 19 years ago.

423
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:26,795
I know.

424
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,839
Oh, my God, we're so old.

425
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:30,883
I'm so grateful for Jason.

426
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:32,092
When I got a divorce,

427
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:35,137
he literally co-signed for an apartment
for me and my kids.

428
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:37,181
I was getting turned down right and left.

429
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:40,517
He was like, "As long as you pay 
the rent on time, it's fine."

430
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:43,353
I've been doing interior design 
for about eight years.

431
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:46,940
I was designing homes and staging homes
for the Oppenheim Group.

432
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:49,818
But now, I literally just got 
my real estate license 

433
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:54,281
and now here I am, trying to learn
everything that they all know.

434
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:56,075
[Jason] Well, this is sexy.

435
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:57,785
-[Mary] This is really nice.
-[Amanza] Whoa!

436
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:01,497
That's not contemporary,
that's a Tuscan Mediterranean.

437
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:02,956
-It's not contemporary.
-Oh!

438
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:03,999
[Jason] Oh.

439
00:18:04,082 --> 00:18:05,959
-Are you okay?
-My shoe is stuck in the thingy.

440
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:07,795
-Oh, my God.
-Did you really get stuck?

441
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:09,963
-[Mary] Leave it to Amanza.
-[Amanza] Oh, my God.

442
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:11,882
[Amanza] It was one of my first meetings

443
00:18:11,965 --> 00:18:14,760
to meet another agent, like,
outside the Oppenheim Group,

444
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:16,345
and I almost bite it.

445
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:19,389
Like, right in front of this 
bougie big-time agent.

446
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:22,351
She got her heel stuck in the deck
at Beverly Glen.

447
00:18:22,434 --> 00:18:23,352
[Mary laughing]

448
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:25,687
-Gotta be the center of attention.
-[Jason laughs]

449
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:27,022
I could've just been barefoot

450
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,732
and been real comfy, you know?
[chuckles]

451
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,109
This would've been easy.

452
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:31,735
-Only me.
-[Shawn] Talk to you later.

453
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:32,736
Okay.

454
00:18:33,111 --> 00:18:35,697
You know the chances of that happening 
are, like, one in a million.

455
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:37,825
-[Amanza] Nice to meet you.
-[Mary] Nice to see you.

456
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:39,827
-I'm the graceful one, Amanza.
-Shawn Elliot.

457
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:42,579
-Nice to meet you. How are you?
-How are you? Good to see you, man.

458
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:43,956
Thank you for getting us up here.

459
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:46,583
[Jason] So we're previewing for a client,
as you know.

460
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,669
We have a celebrity client
looking for privacy.

461
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:51,505
Listen to me, at five million and 750,

462
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:53,674
find me a better house in Bel Air.

463
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:54,800
Doesn't exist.

464
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:56,009
All right, let's take a look.

465
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:59,346
-[Mary] Great.
-[Jason] I like the open kitchen.

466
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:03,142
This island can double as a bar
and you could have a couple bartenders.

467
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:06,728
Guests could line up to get 
their tequila shots, right?

468
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:08,689
-[Mary] How many bedrooms?
-Four bedrooms.

469
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:10,566
And five and a half bathrooms.

470
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:14,236
One of the nicest features of this house
is this open living area.

471
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:16,363
[Jason] This is a nice room.

472
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,157
-[Mary] Wow.
-That's a stunning piano.

473
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,908
-[Shawn] That piano...
