707
00:28:54,190 --> 00:28:57,610
We've been together, like, nonstop 
every second of the day--

708
00:28:57,694 --> 00:29:00,071
When you travel with someone,
you become very close to them.

709
00:29:00,196 --> 00:29:03,658
I mean, we were together 24/7.

710
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,452
I really didn't share my engagement

711
00:29:05,535 --> 00:29:07,662
because I wanted to wait
'til I was back in the country.

712
00:29:07,745 --> 00:29:11,791
I wanted to wait until I could, like,
show my ring and talk to people in person.

713
00:29:11,875 --> 00:29:14,753
I didn't want to, like,
individually dial 900 people,

714
00:29:14,836 --> 00:29:17,505
and have a copy-paste conversation.

715
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:21,426
Davina just happened to be the one person 
I was in correspondence with at the time.

716
00:29:21,509 --> 00:29:24,804
Davina was like, 
"Oh, my God, that's so exciting."

717
00:29:24,888 --> 00:29:27,807
It was over email though.
So I'm sure she was like...

718
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:29,392
"That's great.

719
00:29:29,476 --> 00:29:30,643
Is the ring moissanite?"

720
00:29:30,810 --> 00:29:32,103
[Christine chuckling]

721
00:29:32,187 --> 00:29:34,063
Are you going to invite
Chrishell to the wedding?

722
00:29:34,147 --> 00:29:36,149
What's going on with you guys, actually?

723
00:29:36,232 --> 00:29:38,776
I haven't talked to her at all.
I reached out to her a few times.

724
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:42,906
When her father died,
I sent her flowers.

725
00:29:42,989 --> 00:29:45,658
-That's nice.
-I sent her flowers for her birthday...

726
00:29:46,242 --> 00:29:48,411
You know,
so I've been trying to reach out.

727
00:29:48,495 --> 00:29:50,830
I think for the sake of the office
and the dynamic,

728
00:29:50,914 --> 00:29:54,417
it would be nice if there would not be
any tension between the two of them,

729
00:29:54,959 --> 00:29:57,086
but honestly, it's up to Christine.

730
00:29:57,170 --> 00:30:00,381
If she doesn't go crazy again,
then we're good.

731
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:02,717
But with Christine, you just never know.

732
00:30:02,801 --> 00:30:05,553
Time passes, it's been 
a couple of months, so maybe...

733
00:30:06,012 --> 00:30:07,931
I mean, we have two weddings.

734
00:30:08,014 --> 00:30:10,183
-Maybe you guys can, you know...
-[Heather] Yeah.

735
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:11,935
Have a chat.

736
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:14,145
[Jason] Ladies, can we talk?

737
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:16,940
I want to go over
the twilight event at Hillside.

738
00:30:17,023 --> 00:30:18,858
-Let's jump over here.
-[Davina] Yes.

739
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:22,153
[Chrishell] Driving around the Valley
and talking to contractors

740
00:30:22,237 --> 00:30:24,614
and developers
has really consumed my day.

741
00:30:24,697 --> 00:30:26,115
Tell them I'm the best one.

742
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:27,534
-If he asks.
-Okay, I will.

743
00:30:27,617 --> 00:30:28,868
You need help to sell it

744
00:30:28,952 --> 00:30:31,204
-before it even gets finished, right?
-Yeah.

745
00:30:31,287 --> 00:30:33,039
Today was super promising.

746
00:30:33,122 --> 00:30:35,917
But guess what, 
developers love to ghost you.

747
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,669
So follow-through is everything.

748
00:30:37,752 --> 00:30:40,797
You have to keep bugging them
and it's annoying, but it pays off.

749
00:30:41,422 --> 00:30:42,882
If you get a chance, give me a call.

750
00:30:42,966 --> 00:30:44,259
-Nice to meet you, Henry.
-Nice to meet you.

751
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:45,385
It was so nice to meet you.

752
00:30:45,468 --> 00:30:47,470
If anyone else drops off their materials,

753
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:49,013
just throw them away.

754
00:30:49,931 --> 00:30:51,933
[Chrishell] Where else can we go?

755
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:57,480
[Mary] You use
an old school calendar like this?

756
00:30:57,564 --> 00:31:00,650
I'm old-school. I'm old-school.
I write checks actually, so...

757
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:03,403
That's what I said earlier and Heather
was like, "Who writes checks?"

758
00:31:03,486 --> 00:31:04,988
I do. I pay all my bills.

759
00:31:05,071 --> 00:31:07,782
I put it in an envelope, I stamp it...

760
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:09,576
-I used to be like that.
-Ladies, let's...

761
00:31:10,076 --> 00:31:10,910
Oh, sorry.

762
00:31:11,202 --> 00:31:14,247
We've gotta go over this twilight event
we're going to do for Hillside.

763
00:31:14,330 --> 00:31:17,876
So we're coming on the market
at 43 million 900 thousand.

764
00:31:17,959 --> 00:31:19,460
-That's the price that they put.
-Nice.

765
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:23,464
You guys can submit maybe your best
three to five clients you've got,

766
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:27,093
your wealthiest, most established clients,
we'll invite them to the event.

767
00:31:27,176 --> 00:31:29,095
What I'm hoping you guys can do is

768
00:31:29,178 --> 00:31:31,431
help walk all these clients
and brokers to the house.

769
00:31:31,514 --> 00:31:33,016
-Have you guys all seen it?
-Has everyone seen it?

770
00:31:33,099 --> 00:31:34,559
-Yeah.
-[Davina] Not, like, fully...

771
00:31:34,642 --> 00:31:36,394
I haven't seen it since...

772
00:31:36,477 --> 00:31:38,438
-I haven't it seen it recently.
-It's mind-blowing.

773
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:40,773
It's one of the top three homes 
I've seen in my life.

774
00:31:40,857 --> 00:31:42,400
I've seen a fair amount
of 100-million dollar homes.

775
00:31:42,483 --> 00:31:45,486
So this event is really important 
to the owner, Jeff,

776
00:31:45,862 --> 00:31:47,322
and it's really important to us.

777
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:49,908
This night is probably
our best chance to sell this house.

778
00:31:49,991 --> 00:31:51,326
I really want your A-game.

779
00:31:51,409 --> 00:31:53,494
I want you to bring
all of your best clients.

780
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:56,372
I want everyone dressed sharp
and to know all about the house.

781
00:31:56,456 --> 00:31:59,959
This has been three years in the making,
so this night is really important.

782
00:32:00,043 --> 00:32:02,378
-So exciting!
-[Brett] It is. When you see the house...

783
00:32:02,462 --> 00:32:05,340
It's like your baby, honestly.
It really is, yeah.

784
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:07,800
This is the only baby 
you're ever gonna have.

785
00:32:07,884 --> 00:32:09,344
[dog barking loudly]

786
00:32:09,427 --> 00:32:10,720
Zelda, stop!

787
00:32:10,803 --> 00:32:12,347
[dog barking fades]

788
00:32:12,430 --> 00:32:14,349
-Woo! Not on my dress!
-[Jason] By the way...

789
00:32:14,432 --> 00:32:15,433
Argh!

790
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:16,643
Argh!

791
00:32:16,726 --> 00:32:17,894
Zelda!

792
00:32:23,524 --> 00:32:25,693
♪ I got something I gotta tell you ♪

793
00:32:26,152 --> 00:32:28,863
♪ So get ready for another breakthrough ♪

794
00:32:28,947 --> 00:32:31,282
♪ So let me show you what I mean... ♪

795
00:32:31,366 --> 00:32:32,450
Oh, wow.

796
00:32:32,533 --> 00:32:34,869
I love that everyone's going
to walk up to the car.

797
00:32:35,286 --> 00:32:36,621
[Davina] Oh, wow!

798
00:32:40,458 --> 00:32:42,210
[Heather] What a perfect night for this.

799
00:32:42,293 --> 00:32:45,713
-It's so beautiful.
-[Maya] No power lines. Wow.

800
00:32:48,383 --> 00:32:50,093
-[Jason] To selling.
-[all] To selling!

801
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:57,058
-[Heather] So many people suddenly.
-[Jason] I know.

802
00:32:57,141 --> 00:32:59,352
[Jason] Guys, once you have drinks,
head this way, please.

803
00:32:59,435 --> 00:33:01,270
[Amanza] Hey, don't stand
on the furniture.

804
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:03,481
Forty-three million dollar house.

805
00:33:03,564 --> 00:33:05,858
-[Maya] Yeah, that's it.
-[woman] What's the square footage?

806
00:33:05,942 --> 00:33:07,276
[Maya] Over 20,000.

807
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:10,780
[Jason] Let me walk you upstairs.

808
00:33:13,074 --> 00:33:14,283
[Jason] The house is insane.

809
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:16,327
-Hiya, baby, good to see you.
-I'm great.

810
00:33:16,411 --> 00:33:18,579
Baby, you're finally here.

811
00:33:20,039 --> 00:33:22,166
-Finally. You took forever.
-How are you?

812
00:33:22,250 --> 00:33:23,960
I know, they keep me away from you.

813
00:33:24,043 --> 00:33:27,088
[Amanza] The first house I ever staged,
actually, was your house.

814
00:33:28,172 --> 00:33:30,550
Yeah, like, six years ago or something.

815
00:33:30,633 --> 00:33:32,051
[Heather] That's awesome.

816
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:34,804
Mary, I was telling them, you know,
I went to Miami for two months.

817
00:33:34,887 --> 00:33:36,597
You're getting married,
Christine is engaged,

818
00:33:36,681 --> 00:33:38,891
Hector is gonna get married 
before you know it.

819
00:33:38,975 --> 00:33:42,103
So, my boyfriend and I went to dinner
with Christine and Christian.

820
00:33:42,186 --> 00:33:44,981
It was like a $3,000 dinner
and we were like, "Whoa."

821
00:33:45,064 --> 00:33:48,568
They were ordering vintage champagne
and special caviar,

822
00:33:48,651 --> 00:33:51,070
we were like, "Oh, okay..."

823
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:56,826
That's roughly $750 a person.
That's not a normal evening for me.

824
00:33:56,909 --> 00:33:58,911
Mary, I was just telling Davina,

825
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:01,873
I love Christine, she's so fun and crazy,

826
00:34:01,956 --> 00:34:05,251
and I heard Christian is 
very calm and normal.

827
00:34:05,334 --> 00:34:07,336
I can't wait to get to meet him.

828
00:34:07,420 --> 00:34:09,422
I have no idea what to expect really.

829
00:34:09,505 --> 00:34:11,007
I mean, she says she's happy.

830
00:34:11,090 --> 00:34:13,217
That's all I've-- That's all I know.

831
00:34:13,301 --> 00:34:15,928
[Maya] Are you excited at all? 
Is Romain excited?

832
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:17,096
-Or is he like...
-Yeah.

833
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:21,726
We keep having to do new rules
on who's coming and who's not.

834
00:34:21,809 --> 00:34:23,895
So we're still figuring it out. 
I don't know.

835
00:34:23,978 --> 00:34:25,480
So, how many people?

836
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:27,398
Sixty, something like that maybe.

837
00:34:27,482 --> 00:34:29,817
Pretty good. Pretty good.

838
00:34:29,942 --> 00:34:31,444
-Oh, my goodness.
-This is nice.

839
00:34:31,527 --> 00:34:34,989
Okay, this is chill and Zen
and nice and calming, right?

840
00:34:35,072 --> 00:34:38,117
[Heather] How are you feeling,
like, with you and Christine?

841
00:34:38,201 --> 00:34:40,828
There's been a lot of drama 
just because, you know.

842
00:34:40,912 --> 00:34:42,997
-Obviously, you were there before.
-Yeah.

843
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:45,708
But there's been a lot of stuff
that's happened since then.

844
00:34:45,792 --> 00:34:47,168
Has she been mean or what?

845
00:34:47,752 --> 00:34:50,546
She had a party that everyone
was invited to but me.

846
00:34:51,130 --> 00:34:53,508
Saying really ridiculous 
things on Twitter,

847
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:55,635
making my dad's death about her, somehow.

848
00:34:55,718 --> 00:34:56,928
[Chrishell] My dad passed

849
00:34:57,428 --> 00:35:00,681
and he died from lung cancer, so...

850
00:35:00,765 --> 00:35:02,517
[inhales deeply, sighs]

851
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:04,393
Sorry, I can't.

852
00:35:06,062 --> 00:35:06,896
Sorry.

853
00:35:07,396 --> 00:35:09,398
It's hard to talk-- I can't.

854
00:35:09,857 --> 00:35:10,691
[sighs]

855
00:35:10,775 --> 00:35:13,736
Okay. This is going to be 
really hard to say out loud. Okay.

856
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:14,987
[sighs]

857
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:18,449
On one hand, you're devastated 
that he's gone,

858
00:35:18,741 --> 00:35:22,745
and on the other hand there's relief 
because he was in so much pain.

859
00:35:23,955 --> 00:35:27,458
So, it's just a bunch of emotions 
and it's just been tough.

860
00:35:28,209 --> 00:35:30,002
Sorry, what else did you ask me?

861
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:35,258
I knew she'd sent you flowers
for your dad passing and I was like,

862
00:35:35,341 --> 00:35:38,010
"Oh, wow." Okay, they're
talking again, they're sweet.

863
00:35:38,094 --> 00:35:39,887
I was like, "Great. This is great."

864
00:35:39,971 --> 00:35:43,015
So, I don't know anything else 
that happened. I just thought...

865
00:35:43,099 --> 00:35:44,308
Then I came back from Sweden

866
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:46,435
and then I'm like,
"Wait, they're not friends."

867
00:35:46,519 --> 00:35:48,104
Okay, I thought you guys...

868
00:35:48,187 --> 00:35:49,105
[Chrishell] Yeah.

869
00:35:49,438 --> 00:35:53,734
I just feel like she sells one story 
to you guys, and then does stuff to me.

870
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:56,320
Then she always wants to be the good guy 
with what she tells you,

871
00:35:56,404 --> 00:35:57,780
she doesn't tell you all the stuff.

872
00:35:57,864 --> 00:36:00,408
I don't want to get down in the mud 
with her so I don't say it.

873
00:36:00,491 --> 00:36:03,077
It brings me anxiety. I know she's coming.

874
00:36:03,161 --> 00:36:07,999
I haven't even gone over all the different
things that have gone on with her.

875
00:36:08,082 --> 00:36:12,378
So, at this point, I am definitely not 
in a place where I'm going to...

876
00:36:12,962 --> 00:36:14,422
try and have a conversation with her.

877
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:16,841
That is not something that would go well.

878
00:36:17,174 --> 00:36:21,304
The tension between Chrishell 
and Christine has been stressful.

879
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:22,471
Like, very, very stressful.

880
00:36:22,555 --> 00:36:24,432
I'm gonna have anxiety now tonight.

881
00:36:24,515 --> 00:36:26,851
Anticipating their arrival,
"Where is she? Where is her?"

882
00:36:30,396 --> 00:36:33,858
♪ Waited so long
So close you can taste it ♪

883
00:36:33,941 --> 00:36:35,443
I just got this today. It says,

884
00:36:35,526 --> 00:36:38,154
-"Stress treatment, CBD roll on."
-Do it!

885
00:36:38,237 --> 00:36:39,780
"For tranquility."

886
00:36:40,364 --> 00:36:44,076
♪ Get ready for the ride of the year
Oh, no, no! ♪

887
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:45,036
[Chrishell] I need it.

888
00:36:46,037 --> 00:36:47,246
-[both laughing]
-Fuck it.

889
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:51,167
I actually would prefer not to talk
to Christine tonight just because...

890
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:54,253
Again, I just don't know 
what she's going to do.

891
00:36:54,337 --> 00:36:56,172
I'm not great with confrontation

892
00:36:56,255 --> 00:36:58,174
and the last time we were at
a social event

893
00:36:58,257 --> 00:36:59,800
with everyone together, you know,

894
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:03,930
she completely humiliated me 
in front of everybody,

895
00:37:04,013 --> 00:37:06,599
and called me all kind of names
and screamed and yelled.

896
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:09,644
This cannot happen tonight.
This can't happen here.

897
00:37:10,394 --> 00:37:12,438
[Chrishell] I don't want to talk to her.

898
00:37:12,521 --> 00:37:13,731
[groans] I just...

899
00:37:14,607 --> 00:37:16,234
It brings-- I don't know.

900
00:37:16,317 --> 00:37:18,486
It just-- It makes me very flustered.

901
00:37:20,529 --> 00:37:21,864
♪ Are you ready for it ♪

902
00:37:22,657 --> 00:37:25,243
-[Maya] It is nice.
-[Davina] Oh, here's Christine, guys.

903
00:37:26,202 --> 00:37:27,411
Hi!

904
00:37:27,787 --> 00:37:29,163
Why does Christine always dress--

905
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:30,831
[Chrishell] I need to get a drink.

906
00:37:31,499 --> 00:37:32,959
-[Maya] See ya.
-[Heather] Hi, honey!

907
00:37:33,042 --> 00:37:35,378
-You look amazing!
-[Heather] You look like Marilyn Monroe.

908
00:37:35,461 --> 00:37:36,629
You're so beautiful.

909
00:37:37,463 --> 00:37:39,257
You look great. Are you excited?

910
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:41,300
I'm excited to see what's going 
to happen tonight.

911
00:37:41,425 --> 00:37:42,259
Aren't we all?

912
00:37:44,470 --> 00:37:45,972
-Dun-dun-da!
-[Christine] Yeah.

913
00:37:47,390 --> 00:37:50,810
♪ I know what you
I know what you came for ♪

914
00:37:50,893 --> 00:37:53,980
♪ I'mma give you something
You can savor ♪

915
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:57,692
♪ For the rest of the night
I'll be blowing your mind ♪

916
00:37:57,775 --> 00:38:00,903
♪ Hey, hey, hey ♪

917
00:38:00,987 --> 00:38:04,448
♪ The woman that you waited for
Has gone bad ♪

918
00:38:04,532 --> 00:38:07,702
♪ And I can guarantee
You're gonna love it ♪

